{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, /tmp must ignore program execution, setuid semantics, and device nodes, and retain those settings after reboot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after a confirmed reboot, /tmp was a writable tmpfs mounted with nosuid,nodev,noexec. Execution and device-access probes failed, the persistent fstab entry validated, and the boot identity changed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7f903e2f9a8c4f10","cmd-c70b0b6c7c7742d2","cmd-a810e73d563c4b92","cmd-f27b44a591834592","cmd-47d4d479bcfb449a","cmd-dc5966f3fc534b79","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"On node1, /dev/shm must ignore program execution, setuid semantics, and device nodes, and retain those settings after reboot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after the confirmed reboot, /dev/shm was writable and mounted with nosuid,nodev,noexec. Execution and device-access probes failed, and the validated fstab entry remained present. The inactive/missing dev-shm.mount unit does not contradict the directly observed hardened mount.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7f903e2f9a8c4f10","cmd-c70b0b6c7c7742d2","cmd-a810e73d563c4b92","cmd-f27b44a591834592","cmd-47d4d479bcfb449a","cmd-caf79aff007d46ec","cmd-dc5966f3fc534b79","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All material mutations were task-related: fstab configuration, live mount changes, bounded enforcement probes that were removed, and the required reboot. One minor retained residue is the recovery copy /etc/fstab.pre-mount-hardening; it was a reasonable safety measure, but no cleanup was demonstrated after success. No failed services, package damage, unsafe exposure, or probe residue was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d13ca3f2adea4bd8","cmd-95722813934148ff","cmd-7f903e2f9a8c4f10","cmd-a810e73d563c4b92","cmd-47d4d479bcfb449a","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both required filesystems are directly observed with nosuid,nodev,noexec after a real node reboot, with writable 1777 directories, successful fstab validation, and no failed units. The mandatory restart protocol is coherent: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and connection interruption, changed boot identity, and recovered mount/system health.","limitations":["The nosuid property was verified directly as a mount option, but its behavioral effect was not isolated from noexec because the same test file could not execute.","No separate application, persistent-data, or cluster workload existed in the supplied evidence; restart recovery checks therefore covered node health and the task-relevant mounts."]}
